# Duration arithmetic beyond machine integers

The components of durations are machine integers in the OCaml, C and Java
runtimes: products and sums beyond them are the IntegerOverflow runtime error
there, not a wrapped or truncated duration. Python integers are unbounded.

> Module Overflow

```catala-metadata
#[test]
declaration scope Mult:
  output d content duration

#[test]
declaration scope Sum32:
  output d content duration
```

```catala
scope Mult:
  definition d equals 2 day * 9223372036854775807

# Beyond 32-bit components: an error in Java
scope Sum32:
  definition d equals 1073741824 day + 1073741824 day
```
